## Background

You have been emailed the following environment as is. Turns out that for deployment the client (Ellingson Retro Systems) uses Makefile -s to somewhat automate their Operations Processes.

To be able to test the system exactly as it runs on their production servers, you have been given the following instructions by a user named Ac1d_Burn from the company:

Start with the database first. Hack the planet.

####### DATABASE (THE GIBSON) ###########

# First build the database image from the supplied makefile, just by entering the command:
make
# Then run the container with
make run
# After running this command, your postgres container will be configured with our database.
# There are some handy clean up scripts already provided in the makefile
make clean

####### WEBSERVER (CYBERDELIA) ###########

# First, build the webserver image from the supplied makefile:
make
# Then run the container with
make run
# You should now be able to browse to http://localhost/ to view the wall!

# There are some handy clean up scripts already provided
make clean

# NOTE:

If you have issues getting the basic setup working, ask for help!

# Additional NOTE 1: There should be no space between an option flag and its value.
# Additional NOTE 2: You will get a connection error if you run the 'docker exec' seed step too quickly after starting the database. Wait a few seconds so the database can start.
# HINT: Re-importing the wall every time you start the container is not efficient... how could you make this data persist?
